// Folder-specific settings
//
// For a full list of overridable settings, and general information on folder-specific settings,
// see the documentation: https://zed.dev/docs/configuring-zed#settings-files
{
  // Zed labels our Django templates as plain "HTML", and its default
  // `"formatter": "auto"` resolves that to its bundled Prettier. Prettier has no
  // concept of Django: it treats `{% ... %}` as inline text and re-fills it to
  // printWidth, which happily breaks a tag across two lines. Django's lexer is
  // line-bounded (`tag_re` in django/template/base.py has no re.DOTALL), so a
  // split tag stops being a tag and orphans its closer — that is what produced
  // `TemplateSyntaxError: Invalid block tag ... 'endpartialdef'` on /studio/.
  //
  // djLint is Django-aware and keeps every tag on one line. It reads its config
  // (custom_blocks incl. partialdef, custom_html for cotton's c-* tags) from
  // src/server/djlint.toml — the same tool VS Code already uses here. (That
  // config used to live in src/server/pyproject.toml; it moved out so formatter
  // tweaks stop invalidating the Docker dependency layer.)
  //
  // Paths are relative to the worktree root, which is the cwd Zed runs external
  // formatters in — so this file survives the checkout moving and is safe to
  // commit. (An earlier absolute-path version broke silently when the repo was
  // moved: Zed logs `Formatter failed, skipping` and does NOT fall back to
  // Prettier, so saves simply stopped formatting.)
  //
  // `--configuration` is required and not optional sugar: djLint discovers its
  // config by walking up from the cwd, and the cwd here is the worktree root,
  // one level ABOVE src/server/djlint.toml. Without the flag it silently runs
  // with stock defaults — no custom_blocks, no custom_html.
  //
  // `-` makes djLint read the buffer from stdin and write to stdout, which is
  // what Zed's external formatter expects. Passing `{buffer_path}` as well (as
  // some snippets online do) is a no-op: djLint ignores the extra positional
  // when `-` is present, and it does not affect config discovery.
  "languages": {
    "HTML": {
      "formatter": {
        "external": {
          "command": "src/server/.venv/bin/djlint",
          "arguments": [
            "--reformat",
            "--configuration",
            "src/server/djlint.toml",
            "-"
          ]
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
